## Flow 1: ReportSubmitted — Notify Supervisor on Submission

**Purpose:** When a Contributor submits a monthly report, the responsible Supervisor receives an email alert.

### Prerequisites
- `MonthlyReports` list has a `ReportStatus` column with choice values including `Supervisor Approved`, `Supervisor Rejected`, `M&E Approved`, `M&E Rejected`, `Not Submitted`
- `MonthlyReports` list has a `SubmissionStatus` column with choice values: `Draft`, `Submitted`, `Approved`
- `MonthlyReports` has a lookup/reference to `Activities` (the `Activity` column stores the Activity ID, e.g. `ICMTS-AC-0001`)
- `Activities` list has a `Supervisor` Person column populated with real M365 accounts

### Step 1: Create the Flow

1. Go to **https://make.powerautomate.com**
2. Click **+ Create** in the left sidebar
3. Select **Automated cloud flow**
4. Flow name: `APP-MRMS Report Submitted Notify Supervisor`
5. Trigger: Search for `When an item is created or modified` (SharePoint)
6. Click **Create**

### Step 2: Configure the Trigger

1. **Site Address:** Select your SharePoint site (e.g. `https://yourorg.sharepoint.com/sites/APP-MRMS`)
2. **List Name:** Select `MonthlyReports`
3. Leave all other settings as default
4. Click the **⋯** (three dots) on the trigger card → **Settings**
5. Under **Trigger Conditions**, click **+ Add** and enter:
   ```
   @equals(triggerBody()?['ReportStatus']?['Value'], 'Supervisor Rejected')
   ```
6. Click **+ Add** again and enter:
   ```
   @equals(triggerBody()?['SubmissionStatus']?['Value'], 'Submitted')
   ```
7. Set **Concurrency Control** to **Off** (sequential processing)
8. Click **Done**

> **Why trigger conditions?** Without them, the flow fires on every edit. The trigger conditions ensure it only runs when `SubmissionStatus` changes to `Submitted` OR `ReportStatus` changes to `Supervisor Rejected`.
>
> 📘 **Learn more:** See [`docs/power-automate/trigger-conditions.md`](docs/power-automate/trigger-conditions.md) for the full trigger conditions reference, concurrency control, and polling intervals.

### Step 3: Add "Get Items" to find the Activity

1. Click **+ New step** → Search for `Get items` (SharePoint)
2. **Site Address:** Same SharePoint site
3. **List Name:** Select `Activities`
4. Click **Show advanced options**
5. **Filter Query:**
   ```
   Title eq '@{triggerBody()?['Activity']?['Value']}'
   ```
   > This looks up the Activity by its ID (Title field = Activity ID like `ICMTS-AC-0001`)
>
> 📘 **Learn more:** See [`docs/power-automate/sharepoint-triggers-and-actions.md`](docs/power-automate/sharepoint-triggers-and-actions.md) for all OData filter patterns, Person/Lookup column access, and Get Items reference.

6. **Top Count:** `1`

### Step 4: Send Email to Supervisor

1. Click **+ New step** → Search for `Send an email (V2)` (Office 365 Outlook)
2. **To:** Click in the field, then select **Dynamic content** → Under `Get items`, select `Supervisor Email`
   > If the Supervisor column is empty for this activity, you can add a **Condition** step first to check `Supervisor Email is not equal to null`, and only send if true.

3. **Subject:**
   ```
   Report submitted: @{triggerBody()?['Title']} — @{triggerBody()?['ReportingMonth']?['Value']}
   ```
   > 📘 **Expression reference:** See [`docs/power-automate/expressions-and-functions.md`](docs/power-automate/expressions-and-functions.md) for `triggerBody()`, `concat()`, `formatDateTime()`, and other functions used in these expressions.

4. **Body:** (switch to HTML mode by clicking `</>` icon)
   ```html
   <p><strong>A monthly report has been submitted for your review.</strong></p>
   <table border="1" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse:collapse; font-family:Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif;">
     <tr><td style="background:#f0f0f0;"><strong>Report</strong></td><td>@{triggerBody()?['Title']}</td></tr>
     <tr><td style="background:#f0f0f0;"><strong>Activity</strong></td><td>@{triggerBody()?['Activity']?['Value']}</td></tr>
     <tr><td style="background:#f0f0f0;"><strong>Programme</strong></td><td>@{triggerBody()?['ProgrammeLabel']}</td></tr>
     <tr><td style="background:#f0f0f0;"><strong>Directorate</strong></td><td>@{triggerBody()?['DirectorateLabel']}</td></tr>
     <tr><td style="background:#f0f0f0;"><strong>Reporting Month</strong></td><td>@{triggerBody()?['ReportingMonth']?['Value']}</td></tr>
     <tr><td style="background:#f0f0f0;"><strong>Quarter</strong></td><td>@{triggerBody()?['Quarter']?['Value']}</td></tr>
     <tr><td style="background:#f0f0f0;"><strong>Progress %</strong></td><td>@{triggerBody()?['PercentageComplete']}</td></tr>
     <tr><td style="background:#f0f0f0;"><strong>Submitted By</strong></td><td>@{triggerBody()?['SubmittedBy']?['DisplayName']}</td></tr>
     <tr><td style="background:#f0f0f0;"><strong>Submission Date</strong></td><td>@{triggerBody()?['SubmissionDate']}</td></tr>
   </table>
   <p>Please review this report in the <strong>APP-MRMS</strong> application and approve or reject it.</p>
   <p><em>This is an automated notification from the APP Monthly Reporting Management System.</em></p>
   ```

5. **Importance:** Select `High`

6. Click **Save**

### Step 5: Test

1. Go to your SharePoint `MonthlyReports` list
2. Edit an existing report: set `SubmissionStatus` to `Submitted`
3. Go back to Power Automate → click **Test** → **Manually** → **Test**
4. Wait for the flow to complete (should show green checkmarks)
5. Check the Supervisor's email inbox

